{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2000-05-30T00:00:00+00:00", "updated": "2023-03-07T03:59:22.197566+00:00", "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/527930?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/527930?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/527930?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/527930?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/527930?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/527930?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A527930"}, "metadata": {"authors": [{"full_name": "Bauer, Christian W."}, {"full_name": "Fleming, Sean"}, {"full_name": "Luke, Michael E."}], "publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "63", "artid": "014006", "year": 2000, "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.D"}], "texkeys": ["Bauer:2000ew"], "abstracts": [{"value": "We construct an effective field theory valid for processes in which highly energetic light-like particles interact with collinear and soft degrees of freedom, using the decay B -> X_s + gamma near the endpoint of the photon spectrum, x = 2 E_gamma / m_b -> 1, as an example. Below the scale mu=m_b both soft and collinear degrees of freedom are included in the effective theory, while below the scale mu=m_b sqrt{x-y}, where 1-y is the lightcone momentum fraction of the b quark in the B meson, we match onto a theory of bilocal operators. We show that at one loop large logarithms cancel in the matching conditions, and that we recover the well known renormalization group equations that sum leading Sudakov logarithms."}], "control_number": 527930, "dois": [{"value": "10.1103/PhysRevD.63.014006"}], "arxiv_eprints": [{"value": "hep-ph/0005275"}], "titles": [{"title": "Summing Sudakov logarithms in $B \\to\u00a0 X_s \\gamma $in effective field theory."}], "author_count": 3, "document_type": ["article"]}, "id": "527930"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "